      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think bazel has the ability to do a `locations` of a wildcard in the first place.\n\n```\ngenrule(\n    name \u003d \"foo\",\n    srcs \u003d glob([\"src/**/*.cpp\"]),\n    cmd \u003d \"cat $(locations src/**/*.cpp) \u003e $(out)\",\n    outs \u003d [\"foo.txt\"],\n)\n```\n\n`ERROR: /ssd/test/BUILD.bazel:1:8: in cmd attribute of genrule rule //:foo: label \u0027//:src/**/*.cpp\u0027 in $(locations) expression is not a declared prerequisite of this rule`\n\nHowever I think I agree that it would be better to keep it locked down. I removed this and instead added something to art to fill out their glob.",
